e's nothing visually  that corresponds to it except the  interior state of the actor the  character and it that was a lesson to me  that even on a big Hollywood film where  you think everything is just sort of by  the  book that you can throw these curves  into the soundtrack and actually enhance  the film as a result I was mainly  influenced by the films that were being  made in Europe and Japan India Kurosawa  such abject ray Bergman Fellini Godard  all the 1960s and they sort of charged  me up and that was not only mine but our  goal I would say the same for George  Lucas and Francis Coppola we were all  driven to make films not by so much by  American films but by world cinema if  you had drilled into our minds and said  what do you really want to do it would  be to make films in the United States  but to bring world cinema  in as an influence I love to collaborate  and I've worked on a number of films  where I am one of three editors or one  of two editors one of the real  advantages of digital filmmaking is this  enhancement of the collaborative  back-and-forth you you could do it in  the old days if there were mistakes then  it was hard to sort of pull back you'd  had to reconstitute the film and you  would there were these splices in there  and the expense of reprinting the films  was considerable but it did happen but  the tendency was not to happen but with  the digital stuff there's there's no  reason not to do it the situation is so  different today a machine that could  edit film in Hollywood back then the  movie olla cost the equivalent of forty  two thousand dollars today  whereas today you can take everyone has  a laptop or something or even an iPhone  and you can get editing programs for  free and you can download stuff for free  that the upside of what people have  today  is easy free access to incredible tools  that we just didn't have the downside is  that everybody has access to so the the  amount of competition and how to make  yourself heard in the noise of the  culture today is is that's problematic  but you know you can do something great  and put it on YouTube and get 5 million  hits and there you go you know something  will happen as a result of that  you
 

